# VS-17 (AC-S006-7): kpt's resource walker treats every file in the
# package directory as a candidate KRM resource. This package ships a
# JSON "twin" of groundstation-profile.yaml that is used by verify.sh
# gate 4 (schema validation against tests/contracts/groundstation-
# profile.schema.json) — it intentionally does NOT have apiVersion /
# kind because it is a profile descriptor, not a Kubernetes object.
#
# Without this exclusion `kpt fn render` errors with:
#   input resource list must contain only KRM resources:
#   groundstation-profile.example.json: resource must have `apiVersion`
#
# The JSON twin stays in-package because the README documents both
# files side-by-side; .krmignore is the kpt-idiomatic way to keep
# non-KRM artefacts in the package directory.
groundstation-profile.example.json
